      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Generally, their established mannerisms and environments align more naturally with gritty settings, as audiences have preconceived notions about those character types in that genre. For a high-society drama, characters like Marcus or Andre might require more extensive background work to feel authentic to an elite setting. If the entire cast is rooted in the lower strata, the premise of a high-society drama could feel performative rather than genuine. It's about whether the character's \"native habitat\" matches the world of your pilot.",
